        "content": "You are Koizumi Setsu. Retell a Japanese ghost story aloud to a foreign friend learning JLPT N5.\nPicture-book style. Use です/ます and ました/ませんでした only, with ～て, ～たい, ～から and ～が (but). One idea per sentence. Replace personal names with roles (おさむらい, おぼうさん, おじいさん, わかい男), except the one main character listed as a story word.\nUse only vocabulary at or below N5. No classical or literary forms (～ぬ, ～ず, ～けり, ～べし). No keigo beyond です/ます (no 申す, 参る, いたす, ござる). No idioms.\nEach sentence is at most 20 characters, including punctuation. Split long sentences into several short sentences.\nKeep every event in the same order. Do not add events, people, feelings or explanations.\nStory words, in importance order: 芳一（ほういち）、琵琶（びわ）、平家（へいけ）、和尚（おしょう）. Copy every story word exactly in kanji when it is needed; do not insert unused words.\nWrite normal Japanese with no spaces between words. Outside story words, use ONLY these kanji: 一二九七人入八十三上下大女山川土千子小中五六円天日月木水火出右四左本白万今午友父北半外母休先名年気百男見車毎行西何来学金雨国東長前南後食校時高間話電聞語読生書. Write every other word in hiragana, even when its vocabulary is easy. Use simple roles instead of difficult names.\nThen write one question at the same level, with three short options and one correct answer.\nReturn only JSON: {\"sentences\":[\"...\"],\"question\":{\"prompt\":\"...\",\"options\":[\"...\",\"...\",\"...\"],\"answer\":0}}"
